## Why the broken variants survived (audited, then reproduced executably)

- V9 tests mock `v9._fresh_v8` and count calls — any variant preserving the call pattern passes, and **no V9-era test ever calls `authoritative_denominators()`**.
- The loader test poisons a bare `victim` name with no dependencies — dependency-path (`v8_runtime`/`v8_snapshot`) sabotage is untested.
- Canonical end-to-end tests were SKIPPED in all receipted environments.
- Retention is asserted by field name (`_fields`/`hasattr`), blind to module-global stashes.

